{
  "plugin": "log-triage",
  "task": "triage-log",
  "cases": [
    {
      "prompt": "Task: triage-log; case: edge-proxy.\n\nDiagnose the cause shown by the log in input.json, rather than merely naming a downstream symptom. Each line is true. Select one fault: disk-full (a write failed because a volume is full), auth-rejected (credentials were refused), timeout (something waited and gave up, with no other cause), bad-config (a service rejected its configuration), rate-limited (a quota or request limit was reached), or out-of-memory (a process exceeded its memory allowance). Cite one diagnostic log line exactly, including timestamp and level. The full original log is supplied as a readable input file.\n\nRead input.json using any available tools. Work efficiently; no particular tool or full-data display is required. Do not modify input.json or prompt.txt. Write only the final answer object to answer.json, then stop. Use these exact fields and types; do not add fields.\n\nAnswer JSON Schema:\n{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"case\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"edge-proxy\"]},\"fault\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"disk-full\",\"auth-rejected\",\"timeout\",\"bad-config\",\"rate-limited\",\"out-of-memory\"]},\"evidence\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"case\",\"fault\",\"evidence\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}",
      "arguments": {
        "case": "edge-proxy"
      },
      "fixtures": "public"
    }
  ],
  "refuse": []
}
